ckly, difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education, known to be 100% reliable, creates positive atmosphere with crew. D: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, regarded as arrogant, relatively weak leadership skills.\n\nWe need to compare. Which candidate best fits criteria? Let's weigh.\n\nReliability: C is known 100% reliable. B is very conscientious (reliability). A unknown. D unknown.\n\nStress resilience: B handles stress very well. D responds to unexpected events adequately. A unknown. C unknown.\n\nTechnical competence: B good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills. A sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision. D solves problems extremely well, concentrates. C makes correct decisions quickly.\n\nDecision quality: C makes correct decisions quickly. D solves problems extremely well. A anticipates dangerous situations. B good at weather assessment.\n\nCrew cooperation: C creates positive atmosphere with crew. B can be uncooperative and grumpy. A sometimes not good at taking criticism. D regarded as arrogant, weak leadership.\n\nResponsibility: D takes responsibility seriously. A leadership qualities. B conscientious. C reliable.\n\nOverall, B strong but has cooperation issues (uncooperative, grumpy). C strong reliability, crew atmosphere, decision quality, but egocentric, communication difficulty, not willing to further education. D strong problem solving, responsibility, but arrogance, weak leadership, possibly poor crew cooperation. A strong anticipation, leadership, but unorganized, not good at criticism, maybe poor crew cooperation.\n\nWhich candidate best overall? For long-distance pilot, crew cooperation is crucial. C creates positive atmosphere, but egocentric and communication difficulty may hinder. B's uncooperative and grumpy may be a bigger issue. C's egocentric may also affect. D's arrogance and weak leadership also problematic. A's unorganized and criticism issues also problematic.\n\nReliability: C is 100% reliable, B is conscientious but not explicitly 100% reliable. So C strong.\n\nDecision quality: C quick correct decisions, good for pressure. B not mentioned decision quality.\n\nStress: B handles stress well, D adequate, A unknown, C unknown.\n\nTechnical: B good weather, computer; A spatial vision; D problem solving; C unknown.\n\nOverall, maybe C is best due to reliability, crew atmosphere, decision quality, despite communication issues. But egocentric and unwillingness to further education may affect adaptability. For long-distance, adaptability and learning are important. So maybe B still best.\n\nWe need to make a recommendation. Could either agree with Emily (B) or propose C as stronger alternative. Let's decide to challenge slightly and propose Candidate C as stronger overall due to reliability, decision quality, crew atmosphere, despite communication issues that can be mitigated. Provide evidence.\n\nWe must reference Emily's recommendation. Provide facts: C 100% reliable, creates positive atmosphere, makes correct decisions quickly. Contrast with B's uncooperative and grumpy. Argue that crew cooperation is critical, and C's positive atmosphere outweighs egocentric communication issues, which can be coached.\n\nThus vote for Candidate C.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON with vote Candidate C."}
